{"id":10098,"name":"pikachu-kalos-cap","speciesId":25,"dex":25,"form":"other","generation":1,"types":["electric"],"stats":{"hp":35,"attack":55,"defense":40,"special-attack":50,"special-defense":50,"speed":90},"abilities":[{"name":"static","hidden":false},{"name":"lightning-rod","hidden":true}],"height":4,"weight":60,"baseExp":112,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10098.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/10098.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/10098.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/10098.ogg","genus":"Mouse Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"When several of these POKéMON gather, their electricity could build and cause lightning storms."},{"version":"yellow","text":"It keeps its tail raised to monitor its surroundings. If you yank its tail, it will try to bite you."},{"version":"gold","text":"This intelligent POKéMON roasts hard BERRIES with electricity to make them tender enough to eat."},{"version":"silver","text":"It raises its tail to check its sur­ roundings. The tail is sometimes struck by light­ ning in this pose."},{"version":"crystal","text":"When it is anger­ ed, it immediately discharges the energy stored in the pouches in its cheeks."},{"version":"ruby","text":"Whenever PIKACHU comes across something new, it blasts it with a jolt of electricity. If you come across a blackened berry, it’s evidence that this POKéMON mistook the intensity of its charge."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"This POKéMON has electricity-storing pouches on its cheeks. These appear to become electrically charged during the night while PIKACHU sleeps. It occasionally discharges electricity when it is dozy after waking up."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It stores electricity in the electric sacs on its cheeks. When it releases pent-up energy in a burst, the electric power is equal to a lightning bolt."},{"version":"firered","text":"It has small electric sacs on both its cheeks. If threatened, it looses electric charges from the sacs."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"When several of these POKéMON gather, their electricity can build and cause lightning storms."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It lives in forests with others. It stores electricity in the pouches on its cheeks."},{"version":"pearl","text":"If it looses crackling power from the electric pouches on its cheeks, it is being wary."},{"version":"platinum","text":"It occasionally uses an electric shock to recharge a fellow PIKACHU that is in a weakened state."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"This intelligent Pokémon roasts hard berries with electricity to make them tender enough to eat."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"It raises its tail to check its surroundings. The tail is sometimes struck by lightning in this pose."},{"version":"black","text":"It occasionally uses an electric shock to recharge a fellow Pikachu that is in a weakened state."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Whenever Pikachu comes across something new, it blasts it with a jolt of electricity. If you come across a blackened berry, it’s evidence that this Pokémon mistook the intensity of its charge."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"This Pokémon has electricity-storing pouches on its cheeks. These appear to become electrically charged during the night while Pikachu sleeps. It occasionally discharges electricity when it is dozy after waking up."},{"version":"sun","text":"A plan was recently announced to gather many Pikachu and make an electric power plant."},{"version":"moon","text":"It’s in its nature to store electricity. It feels stressed now and then if it’s unable to fully discharge the electricity."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"Its nature is to store up electricity. Forests where nests of Pikachu live are dangerous, since the trees are so often struck by lightning."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"While sleeping, it generates electricity in the sacs in its cheeks. If it’s not getting enough sleep, it will be able to use only weak electricity."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"This forest-dwelling Pokémon stores electricity in its cheeks, so you’ll feel a tingly shock if you touch it."},{"version":"sword","text":"Pikachu that can generate powerful electricity have cheek sacs that are extra soft and super stretchy."},{"version":"shield","text":"When Pikachu meet, they’ll touch their tails together and exchange electricity through them as a form of greeting."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"Possesses cheek sacs in which it stores electricity. This clever forest-dweller roasts tough berries with an electric shock before consuming them."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":190,"eggGroups":["ground","fairy"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"pichu","speciesId":172,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Felicidade alta"],"species":"pikachu","speciesId":25,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Usar Thunder Stone","Usar Thunder Stone"],"species":"raichu","speciesId":26,"evolvesTo":[]}]}]},"varieties":[{"id":25,"name":"pikachu","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/25.png"},{"id":10080,"name":"pikachu-rock-star","form":"other","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10080.png"},{"id":10081,"name":"pikachu-belle","form":"other","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10081.png"},{"id":10082,"name":"pikachu-pop-star","form":"other","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10082.png"},{"id":10083,"name":"pikachu-phd","form":"other","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/offi